    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 3 tests green (that's the only test class in the repo).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change introduces address normalization on owner creation, mirroring the existing telephone-normalization idiom (mapper `@Named` qualifier delegating to a small util class), keeping all edits out of the large `Owner` and controller classes.\n\n**Files touched (2):**\n\n1. **New `util/Addresses.java`** \u2014 a tiny, self-contained normalizer (`normalize`): trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Null-safe like its sibling `E164`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"address\", qualifiedByName = \"normalizeAddress\")` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` plus a one-line `normalizeAddress` default method, exactly parallel to `normalizeTelephone`.\n\n**Why nothing else needed changing:**\n- *Store & return normalized*: `addOwner` maps the incoming DTO via `toOwner`, so the persisted (and returned) address is normalized.\n- *Household duplicate detection & shared household id*: these read `owner.getAddress()`, which is now the stored normalized value, and `Households.normalize` is applied consistently to both sides \u2014 so comparisons already use the normalized form without editing that class.\n- *Required-field check rejects blank-after-normalization*: whitespace-only input fails the DTO's `.*\\S.*` pattern and is rejected with 400 (confirmed by the `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize` test), and normalization can never turn a non-blank value blank.\n\nStructural impact stayed low: the new logic lives in a class with no surrounding methods (WMC_other = 0), and the mapper edits are small additions to an interface with minimal surrounding complexity \u2014 the big `Owner` entity and the owner controller were left untouched.",
